//@ run-pass
//@ timeout: 300
//@ expect-stdout-contains: M2_HIERARCHICAL_PRIOR_PASS
//@ known-failure: measured 2026-09-22 under SOUNIO_SOUC_ENGINE=lean_single, POST-FIX
//   (see HISTORY note below) -- rel_Hess_individual=0.191766 and
//   rel_Hess_population=0.194044, both still past the 0.10 criterion
//   (M2_HIERARCHICAL_PRIOR_OUTPUT, not _PASS). This is now a genuine,
//   independently-corroborated numerical-methods finding, not a bug: the
//   second-order Hessian GUM approximation does not converge to within 10%
//   of Monte Carlo for this hierarchical eta/epsilon decomposition of the
//   rapamycin PBPK28 AUC endpoint at CV~30-40%. It is consistent with the
//   SAME endpoint's single-level Hessian-vs-MC residual measured elsewhere
//   in this codebase (mc28_selftest_main in pbpk28_mc_cross_validation.sio:
//   ~0.175; pbpk28_m5_gum_4th_order.sio's rel_hess_residual: 0.175404),
//   i.e. a repeatable ~17-19% gap for this convex (AUC ~ 1/CL-dominated)
//   endpoint at this uncertainty magnitude, not an artifact of the
//   hierarchical decomposition specifically. bin/llm-offload -t math-review
//   -p xai (.claude/llm_offload_log.md, 2026-09-22 entry) confirmed this
//   reading is defensible and that the 0.10 gate should NOT be loosened to
//   make the test pass -- it is left as known-failure on purpose, per this
//   repo's policy against retrofitting tolerances to observed failures.
//
// HISTORY (2026-09-22): this test was previously known-failure with much
// larger numbers (rel_Hess_individual=0.875070, rel_Hess_population=
// 0.873336, u_Hessian_individual=0.275193 vs u_MC_individual=2.202779
// mg.h/L, MC mean AUC individual=2.631366 mg.h/L -- well outside the
// codebase's own [0.1, 10.0] mg.h/L plausibility window once the Hessian
// value is used as the reference). Root cause: NOT the hierarchical
// modeling assumption, NOT a wrong MC aggregation -- a lean_single
// compiler miscompile in darwin_pbpk::validation::pbpk28_mc_cross_validation
// ::mc28_exp (this module's own Taylor-series exp(), used throughout
// mc28_sample_hier_lognormal's actual Monte Carlo sampling and by
// mc28_prior_with_logvar). mc28_exp used a "n_f = x*inv_ln2; n = n_f as
// i64; if (n as f64) > n_f { n = n-1 }" floor-then-power-of-2-loop range
// reduction that lean_single miscompiles: the power-of-2 while loop runs
// at ~2x its correct trip count regardless of whether the correcting
// if-branch is taken. Every one of the 7 physiological parameter means in
// this model (12.4, 0.3, 0.08, 0.10, 5.40, 4.20, 0.30) requires at least
// one doubling in range reduction (|ln(mean)| >= ln2 for all of them), so
// essentially every Monte Carlo draw in mc28_run_hierarchical was corrupted
// by a parameter-dependent multiplicative factor (confirmed via minimal
// repro: mc28_exp(ln(12.4)) returned 99.2 instead of 12.4, exactly
// 2^3 doubled to 2^6). Fixed by replacing mc28_exp's range reduction with
// the already-correct iterative form used by ms28_exp in
// pbpk28_mc_prior_family_sweep.sio (independently verified not to trigger
// the bug), reviewed per bin/llm-offload -t math-review -p xai. Post-fix
// cross-checks outside this test's own gate: the fixed single-level MC
// baseline (mc28_selftest_main) now reproduces u_MC=0.357945, an exact
// match (6 significant figures) to the hardcoded M6-canonical MC-truth
// constant already used in cumulants.sio's m5_pbpk28_convergence_budget();
// MC mean AUC individual/population (1.076898 / 1.153652 mg.h/L) are now
// inside the codebase's own physically-plausible [0.1, 10.0] mg.h/L
// window.
// mc28_hierarchical_selftest_main prints M2_HIERARCHICAL_PRIOR_OUTPUT (not
// _PASS) when individual_pass is false, but then unconditionally prints
// PASS and returns 0 regardless -- an unannotated run-pass file only checks
// the exit code, so without this it would report success even when the
// hierarchical-prior criterion actually failed. Requiring the real success
// marker closes that.
// tests/run-pass/pbpk28_m2_hierarchical_prior.sio
//
// Opt-in wrapper for PBPK28 M2 hierarchical eta/epsilon prior decomposition.
// The canonical single-level MC cross-validation remains the default main in
// stdlib/darwin_pbpk/validation/pbpk28_mc_cross_validation.sio.

use darwin_pbpk::validation::pbpk28_mc_cross_validation::{mc28_hierarchical_selftest_main}

fn main() -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    mc28_hierarchical_selftest_main()
}
